From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zaid <283011337+nottzaid@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Cascaded shadow maps

Directional lights cast through three cascaded shadow maps (2048^2,
practical splits to 100 m, sphere-fitted and texel-snapped, hardware
PCF) instead of stencil volumes: any mesh size, alpha masks included.
Instanced casters are culled per cascade at the viewer's level of
detail. Far cascades are reused until the view leaves them; the near
one redraws every frame. Alpha-masked casters keep each shadow texel
with probability equal to their coverage (a hard cutoff where texels
are resolved), so filtered lookups pass light through foliage; a
boosted cutoff made crowns opaque.

Replaces these patches of the numbered series, with what each measured
as it landed (tools/profile_forest.py, GTX 1060 3 GB, i5-4670):
- 0011-cascaded-shadow-maps: frame 5.7 -> 12.3 ms; brightness vs Cycles
  1.4-2.3x -> 1.15-1.96x
- 0027-stochastic-shadow-alpha: main sun under the canopy vs Cycles
  0.30x -> 0.79x
